Carolina to a 20-17 victory over South Florida on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5075800/emory-williams\" target=\"_new\">Emory Williams</a> threw two touchdown passes to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5122006/landon-sides\" target=\"_new\">Landon Sides</a> for East Carolina.\n\n\r\n              The Pirates had the advantage in a matchup of two top-50 defenses, holding the Bulls to 329 total yards. East Carolina had 361 total yards.\n\n\r\n              Williams' 15-yard touchdown pass to Sides in the final minute of the second quarter lifted the Pirates into a 10-10 tie at halftime.\n\n\r\n              Their second connection — an 8-yarder — gave the Pirates a 17-10 lead with 6 1/2 minutes left in the third quarter. South Florida tied it at 17 on <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5154559/jason-collins-jr\" target=\"_new\">Jason Collins Jr</a>.'s 1-yard run with about 10 minutes left in the fourth.\n\n\r\n              The Bulls scored on their opening possession on a 26-yard pass from <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5079542/luke-kromenhoek\" target=\"_new\">Luke Kromenhoek</a> to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870927/bryson-rodgers\" target=\"_new\">Bryson Rodgers</a> but did not find the end zone again until the fourth quarter.\n\n\r\n              Williams completed 19 of 27 passes for 175 yards. Sides caught 14 passes for 126 yards and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5194306/ashton-gray\" target=\"_new\">Ashton Gray</a> ran for 101 yards for the Pirates (5-4, 3-2 American Conference).\n\n\r\n              Kromenhoek was 17-for-21 passing for 179 yards and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5085507/dj-crowther\" target=\"_new\">D.J. Crowther</a> ran for 111 yards for South Florida (6-3, 2-3).\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              South Florida: vs. Memphis on Thursday.\n\n\r\n              East Carolina: at Charlotte on Nov. 14.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-07T04:34:33Z"}}